  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Dakota has received $793M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 2,556 awards with an average award size of $310K, and obligations fell 3.4% year over year. Year-to-year obligations have varied: FY21 was $780M, FY22 was $973M, FY23 was $803M, FY24 was $980M, and FY25 was $821M. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer with $353M in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $193M and the Department of Transportation with $88.3M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the largest vendor with $328M in obligations, while WALSH FEDERAL LLC follows with $74.4M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations at $291M. This snapshot reflects federal buying patterns in North Dakota for FY2026 to date. Use these figures to prioritize agency engagement, target the largest vendors for partnerships, or align capability statements with the biggest industries and contract sizes in the state.",
